{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1657"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",50],["-","history."],["+","history,"],["=",1],["+","and some of its catchiest hits. "],["=",750],["+","Not every name came from the library. The Cure began in Crawley in 1976 as Malice, became Easy Cure, after a song by the drummer Lol Tolhurst, and in 1978 shortened that to The Cure. Under Robert Smith the band moved from the bleak gothic records of the early 1980s to perfect pop and conquered the charts with songs such as „The Love Cats“ (1983) and „Friday I'm in Love“ (1992).\n\nThe Psychedelic Furs, formed in London in 1977 around the brothers Richard and Tim Butler, took their „Furs“ from the Velvet Underground song „Venus in Furs“. Their 1981 song „Pretty in Pink“ gave its name to John Hughes's 1986 film starring Molly Ringwald, and the band re-recorded it as the film's title song.\n\n"],["=",147],["+","\n| The Cure | \"Easy Cure\", a song by Lol Tolhurst | Crawley, 1976 |\n| The Psychedelic Furs | \"Venus in Furs\" (Velvet Underground) | London, 1977 |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",44],["-","hervor."],["+","hervor"],["=",1],["+","– und einige ihrer eingängigsten Hits. "],["=",744],["+","Nicht jeder Name stammte aus der Bibliothek. The Cure begannen 1976 in Crawley als Malice, wurden zu Easy Cure – nach einem Lied des Schlagzeugers Lol Tolhurst – und kürzten das 1978 zu The Cure. Unter Robert Smith wandte sich die Band von den düsteren Gothic-Platten der frühen 1980er-Jahre dem perfekten Pop zu und eroberte die Charts mit Liedern wie „The Love Cats“ (1983) und „Friday I'm in Love“ (1992).\n\nThe Psychedelic Furs, 1977 in London um die Brüder Richard und Tim Butler gegründet, nahmen ihre „Furs“ aus dem Velvet-Underground-Lied „Venus in Furs“. Ihr Lied „Pretty in Pink“ von 1981 gab John Hughes' Film von 1986 mit Molly Ringwald den Namen, und die Band nahm es als Titelsong des Films neu auf.\n\n"],["=",139],["+","\n| The Cure | „Easy Cure“, ein Lied von Lol Tolhurst | Crawley, 1976 |\n| The Psychedelic Furs | „Venus in Furs“ (Velvet Underground) | London, 1977 |"]]}]},
